/**
 * RELEASING: flip this in code (`false ||` below to `true ||`), never with VITE_NEXT_WORLD or NEXT_WORLD in the
 * environment. The online server reads the environment when it starts, so an env-flipped client and a server
 * without the variable make two worlds and the server refuses every new game. scripts/releaseInfo.mjs enforces it:
 * npm run package and npm run online refuse an env-flipped build, a 0.7.x label with the flag off (or a 0.6.x one
 * with it on), and the deployed server will not start beside a game of another GEN (server/index.ts main).
 *
 * The next world: everything that changes how counties are generated and so starts the online world again,
 * held back for the release that does that (0.7.0, GEN_VERSION 53). Off, every county is GEN 52's to the tile.
 * Flip NEXT_WORLD to true with that release, and with it go:
 * - GEN_VERSION 52 → 53 (world/generate.ts)
 * - AVOID_LOTS: roads kept off buildings' lots (world/roads.ts)
 * - the six ancient wonders: the Colossus, the Pharos, the Hanging Gardens, the Temple of Artemis, the Statue
 *   of Zeus and the Mausoleum (world/ancientKinds.ts, placed by generate.ts through world/wonders.ts)
 * - a wonder's approach road may bridge a river, as a road between towns does (world/links.ts linkWorks)
 * - the Adriatic town style: a Rovinj on about a third of warm seaside villages, suburbs and cities that are not
 *   canal towns, its harbour dug in from the sea (world/canals.ts ADRIATIC_CHANCE, `harbour`; world/towns.ts
 *   `adriatic`; render/buildings/adriatic.ts); off, it is never rolled
 * - places to play: an elementary school (a playground beside it) in most towns, go-kart tracks and archery ranges
 *   (world/playKinds.ts, placed by world/towns.ts playSites)
 * - ranches: a named arch and a homestead yard on the edge of a great fenced pasture in the open grass country,
 *   its herd of cattle or horses penned inside with a rider among them (world/ranches.ts, placed last by generate.ts;
 *   game/herds.ts spawnRanches; `npm run ranches`); off, none is placed and the Ranch landform label is left out
 * - city plans (docs/cityplans.html, world/plans): every big city, megalopolis and some small cities laid out to one
 *   of 35 plans beside its style (the Eixample, L'Enfant's Washington, Haussmann's étoiles, Edo's spiral, the Finger
 *   Plan…), with the water, lakes, parks, arms and four-lane diagonals they cut and lay; the town card's plan line and
 *   the Town Planner deed (`npm run cityplans`); off, every town is laid out as today and no plan is rolled
 * - onsen towns (docs/onsen.html, world/onsen.ts): about a quarter of the villages, suburbs and small cities on wooded or
 *   hilly ground built as one of Japan's hot-spring towns (Hakone, Kusatsu, Kinosaki, Ginzan, Beppu, Dōgo): a stream cut
 *   through the square, ryokan in four builds along it (the Fukuzumirō among them), Dōgo's grand bathhouse, the
 *   yubatake, the hells, foot baths, the ropeway and the lake torii, steam rising everywhere (`npm run onsen`); off,
 *   none is rolled and no onsen kind is listed
 * - lake towns (docs/lakes.html, world/lakes.ts): about one in five villages, suburbs and small cities on green, temperate
 *   ground wrapped round a big lake cut in the square and running off out of town, after West Okoboji (cottages, the
 *   amusement park, pontoon docks), Geneva Lake (Gilded Age estates on the shore path), Lac Léman (palace hotels, the
 *   Jet d'Eau, Chillon, paddle steamers) or Lake Como (pastel villas terraced to the water, Riva launches, ferries):
 *   the lakeshore drive, steamer landings, docks, boathouses and bathing beaches, boats on the lake (`npm run lakes`);
 *   off, none is rolled and no lake kind is listed
 * - two-runway internationals (docs/rides.html, world/airportPlans.ts): two in three megalopolis airports, where they
 *   fit, get a second full-length runway at right angles, crossing the first (X) or meeting it at a corner (L), one
 *   apron and two stands shared, one runway lock (`npm run airports2`); off, every international has one runway
 *
 * To try it before then, start a dev server with VITE_NEXT_WORLD=1, or run a node gate with NEXT_WORLD=1:
 * neither is set anywhere a release is built.
 */
// Vite replaces `import.meta.env` (the cast is only for the server's tsconfig, which has no Vite types and is
// erased before Vite reads the code); a node bundle has none, hence the `?.`
const viteEnv = (import.meta as { env?: Record<string, string | undefined> }).env;
const nodeEnv = (globalThis as { process?: { env?: Record<string, string | undefined> } }).process?.env;

export const NEXT_WORLD: boolean = true || viteEnv?.VITE_NEXT_WORLD === '1' || nodeEnv?.NEXT_WORLD === '1';

/**
 * The world after that one, held for 0.8.0 (GEN_VERSION 54) the same way: flip `false ||` to `true ||` in code with
 * that release, never in the environment (try it with VITE_NEXT_080=1 / NEXT_080=1). With it go:
 * - rail-side works (world/railside.ts): a lumber siding, coal loader, tank farm, stockyard, cement loadout, inland
 *   port, mail depot, ballast pit, produce shed and brewery siding standing beside the line, each making or taking
 *   its own goods for the trains (the user, 28 Oct 2026)
 * - the undersea works (world/undersea.ts): pearl beds, a research habitat, a drowned village, a cable junction, a vent
 *   field, a nodule field, a reef observatory and a listening post on the seabed, for a submarine; a kelp farm and
 *   salmon pens at the surface, for any boat
 * - double track on the trunk lines (world/railPlan.ts twinPath, the user, 3 Nov 2026): a second track beside every
 *   trunk, each one-way (keep left), an island platform at every station serving both, a rung's end merging onto the
 *   near track with a crossover over from the far one (a single-lead junction); the dispatcher keeps every train to its
 *   own track's way (game/trains.ts allowed) and never holds one-way line against itself (`NEXT_080=1 npm run doubletrack`)
 * Off, none is placed and every county is GEN 53's to the tile.
 */
export const NEXT_080: boolean = false || viteEnv?.VITE_NEXT_080 === '1' || nodeEnv?.NEXT_080 === '1';
